# waysconf.szymonpaluch.com — one address for the whole session.
#
# The deck and the finished festival site are folders on this site, /deck/ and /site/, built
# with their base set to those paths by scripts/build-subpaths.mjs. The hub does not link to
# them until they are unlocked (UNLOCK=… node scripts/build-guideline.mjs), but they are here.
#
# No rule for /deck or /site without the slash: Netlify ignores a trailing slash when it
# matches a rule, so "/deck → /deck/" would redirect to itself for ever. Its pretty URLs add
# the slash on their own.

# The deck is a single-page app with history routes: /deck/12 is slide 12, and there is no
# file called 12. A real file under /deck/ is served as it is — Netlify only applies a 200
# rewrite when nothing exists at the path — and everything else is the deck's own page.
/deck/*    /deck/index.html                        200

# The prompts page moved when the site was split into two tabs. Anyone holding the old
# link — it was in an early draft of the organiser email — lands in the right place.
/prompts   /workshop/                              301
/prompts/* /workshop/                              301
